From 16e82a82fbdb7c8565d2aa15e014ca87c3d6620c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:14:53 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak of collected items left on a screen

screen_write_collect_flush_line() writes out the part of each collected
item that is visible and leaves the rest collected, so a line can still
hold items when the screen is freed -- there is nothing in front of the
flush that promises it emptied the list. screen_write_free_list() freed
the lines' text and the array and dropped whatever was still on them.

A zero-width screen is the easy way to see it: format_draw() sizes its
screens by the length of the string, so drawing an empty format gives
each one the clear item screen_write_clearendofline() collected and no
column to write it in. A server drawing an empty status format ten times
exits under AddressSanitizer with

    Direct leak of 384 byte(s) in 4 object(s) allocated from:
        #2 screen_write_get_citem screen-write.c:73
        #3 screen_write_init screen-write.c:358
        #4 screen_write_start screen-write.c:401
        #5 format_draw format-draw.c:748

and none with this applied. The items go back to the free list they came
from, which is also what a screen_resize() through free_list/make_list
should do with them rather than losing them.

Applies to 3.7b unchanged but for the offset; the function is the same
there.
---
 screen-write.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/screen-write.c b/screen-write.c
--- a/screen-write.c
+++ b/screen-write.c
@@ -289,10 +289,18 @@ screen_write_make_list(struct screen *s)
 void
 screen_write_free_list(struct screen *s)
 {
-	u_int	y;
+	struct screen_write_cline	*cl;
+	struct screen_write_citem	*ci, *ci1;
+	u_int				 y;
 
-	for (y = 0; y < screen_size_y(s); y++)
-		free(s->write_list[y].data);
+	for (y = 0; y < screen_size_y(s); y++) {
+		cl = &s->write_list[y];
+		TAILQ_FOREACH_SAFE(ci, &cl->items, entry, ci1) {
+			TAILQ_REMOVE(&cl->items, ci, entry);
+			screen_write_free_citem(ci);
+		}
+		free(cl->data);
+	}
 	free(s->write_list);
 }
 
